---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title={"Advancing ATE Strategy For mmWave Mass Market Production | Roos Instruments"}
  description={"Even at mmWave frequencies, Cassini matches the performance of the bench-top\n                        units they typically replace.  Cassini's modular configuration is focused on precise calibration,\n                        low loss device connections and high measurement accuracy with a small footprint and low capital expense."}
  active={["nav-company"]}>
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <meta name="keywords" content="mmWave mass market production, Automated Test Equipment, ATE strategies, article, microwave journal, IoT, SoC, SiP, Cassini modular architecture, precise calibration, low-loss device connections, high measurement accuracy, future-proof features, scalable testing, high-frequency applications, cost-effective solution, Roos Instruments">
  </Fragment>
        <!-- ==========================
    	BREADCRUMB - START
    =========================== -->
        <section class="breadcrumb-wrapper">
            <div class="container">
                <h2>Advancing ATE Strategy For mmWave Mass Market Production</h2>

                <ol class="breadcrumb">
                    <li><a href="/index.html">Home</a></li>
                    <li><a href="/company.html">Company</a></li>
                    <li class="active">Microwave Journal - March 2020</li>
                </ol>
            </div>
        </section>
        <!-- ==========================
    	BREADCRUMB - END
    =========================== -->

        <div id="content" class="roosC container">
            <div class="row">
                <div class="col-sm-4">
                    <h1>mmWave ATE - Microwave Journal Article</h1>
                    <p style="text-align: center;">
                        <a class="btn btn-primary btn-lg" href="/pdf/MicrowaveJournal_March2020-Advancing-mmWave.pdf"><i
                                class="far fa-file-pdf" aria-hidden="true"></i>Read Article</a>
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        <a href="/pdf/MicrowaveJournal_March2020-Advancing-mmWave.pdf">
                            <img src="/images/mmwave_article_thumbnail.png"
                                alt="Microwave Journal March 2020 Techical Feature">
                        </a>
                    </p>
                    <p>The automated test and measurement landscape is rapidly changing, progressing
                        beyond the capabilities of traditional bench-top and most legacy
                        <abbr title="Automated Test Equipment">ATE</abbr> systems. Varying and
                        diverse performance requirements, testing speeds and frequencies used by modern cellular
                        architectures (5G), Internet-of-Things (IoT) devices, and the latest feature dense
                        systems-on-chip/systems-in-package (SoC/SiP) necessitate a different approach.
                    </p>
                    <p style="text-align: right;"> <a href="/company.html#ceo">Mark Roos</a><br>
                        <i>Roos Instruments, CEO</i>
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        <i class="fa-solid fa-link fa-sm"></i>
                        <a target="_blank"
                            href="https://www.microwavejournal.com/articles/33612-advancing-ate-strategy-for-mmwave-mass-market-production?page=1">
                            Visit MicrowaveJournal.com</a>
                        <span class="quiet"><br> (free registration needed)</span>
                        <span class="hidden"><br>
                            <i class="fa-solid fa-link"></i> <a
                                href="https://digital.microwavejournal.com/?issueID=29&pageID=58" target="_new">Visit
                                the
                                online edition</a>* of Microwave Journal March 2020 (page
                            58)<br></span>
                    </p>
                </div>
                <div class="col-sm-8">
                    <hr class="space">
                    <h3>From Bench to Cassini</h3>
                    <p> Cassini leverages a modular configuration focused on precise calibration, low loss device
                        connections and high measurement accuracy with a small footprint and low capital expense.
                        Cassini's Modular architecture can provide future proof features and enable
                        <abbr title="Automated Test Equipment">ATE</abbr> systems to be faster and more accurate with
                        less development. Even at mmWave frequencies, Cassini matches the performance of the bench-top
                        units they typically replace.
                    </p>
                    <a href="/products.html">Learn more about Cassini</a>
                    <p>
                        <a href="/products.html">
                            <img src="/images/legacy_to_production.png" title="Legacy to Production">
                        </a>
                    </p>
                    <hr class="space">
                    <p style="text-align: right;">
                        Start by sending us your device's test list today. &nbsp;
                        <a class="btn-primary btn-lg" href="mailto:sales@roos.com"><i class="fa-solid fa-envelope"
                                aria-hidden="true"></i>&nbsp;&nbsp;Email Sales</a> &nbsp;
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <!-- end .row -->
        </div>
</Base>
